WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:01.735
You served in the Trump administration.

00:00:01.735 --> 00:00:02.702
I have to ask you about

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:04.270
the news of the day,

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:05.238
the news that former

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:06.906
President Trump has posted on truth,

00:00:06.906 --> 00:00:08.041
social

00:00:08.041 --> 00:00:09.009
justice this morning,

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:11.211
that he expects to be arrested on Tuesday

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:13.446
and is also calling for protests,

00:00:13.446 --> 00:00:15.115
telling his supporters to, quote,

00:00:15.115 --> 00:00:16.449
take our nation back.

00:00:16.449 --> 00:00:17.851
Your thoughts?

00:00:18.985 --> 00:00:20.420
Well, just to explain,

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:21.755
if he is about to be arrested,

00:00:21.755 --> 00:00:23.056
it almost certainly means he's

00:00:23.056 --> 00:00:24.357
going to be indicted first.

00:00:24.357 --> 00:00:25.859
He's going to be required to come in

00:00:25.859 --> 00:00:27.293
and surrender himself

00:00:27.293 --> 00:00:28.695
to answer to the indictment.

00:00:28.695 --> 00:00:30.897
So it's not some random decision.

00:00:31.664 --> 00:00:34.734
I strongly believe in a free society.

00:00:34.734 --> 00:00:36.302
There's got to be one rule of law

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:37.537
for everybody.

00:00:37.537 --> 00:00:38.872
I think that's clear.

00:00:38.872 --> 00:00:41.041
I don't know how you make that judgment

00:00:41.441 --> 00:00:42.942
when you're talking about a case

00:00:42.942 --> 00:00:43.943
involving somebody

00:00:43.943 --> 00:00:44.911
paying hush money

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:47.347
to a prostitute or a stripper.

00:00:47.347 --> 00:00:49.082
I only know one person

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:49.983
who's ever done that.

00:00:49.983 --> 00:00:50.817
I worked for him.

00:00:50.817 --> 00:00:53.686
It's a kind of strange situation.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.021
But I'll say this,

00:00:55.021 --> 00:00:56.923
however guilty Trump may be

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.792
and having very much in mind

00:00:58.792 --> 00:01:01.161
the one rule of law for everybody,

00:01:01.161 --> 00:01:02.629
if they indict

00:01:02.629 --> 00:01:05.231
and failed a convict in New York,

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:07.033
I think historians would look back

00:01:07.033 --> 00:01:09.102
and say that is the act that reelected

00:01:09.102 --> 00:01:10.203
Donald Trump president.

00:01:10.203 --> 00:01:12.539
So I hope those prosecutors in New York

00:01:12.806 --> 00:01:15.575
are very, very certain of their case.

00:01:16.776 --> 00:01:18.912
Well, I've opined here that in the

00:01:18.912 --> 00:01:20.213
the four buckets

00:01:20.213 --> 00:01:22.115
that I perceive where he faces

00:01:22.115 --> 00:01:23.716
legal peril.

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:25.318
This is, in my opinion,

00:01:25.318 --> 00:01:26.252
the weakest of them.

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.153
And I have to believe

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:28.922
that there's a risk here of this

00:01:28.922 --> 00:01:30.990
taint might not be the right word,

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.459
but tainting the prosecutions

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:34.627
that theoretically could follow.

00:01:34.627 --> 00:01:36.262
He's got a right to vigorously

00:01:36.262 --> 00:01:37.564
defend himself against this

00:01:37.564 --> 00:01:39.766
and any other charges that might flow.

00:01:39.766 --> 00:01:41.000
What I don't like

00:01:41.000 --> 00:01:42.569
is him calling for protests,

00:01:42.569 --> 00:01:43.369
because to me, it's

00:01:43.369 --> 00:01:46.539
reminiscent of January six

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:49.309
Well, I think this is an important issue,

00:01:49.309 --> 00:01:50.643
but my own view on January

00:01:50.643 --> 00:01:52.612
the sixth is it was not an insurrection.

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:53.513
It was a riot.

00:01:53.513 --> 00:01:54.881
It was one of the saddest days

00:01:54.881 --> 00:01:55.748
in American history,

00:01:55.748 --> 00:01:57.283
but it was not an attempted coup

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:59.119
because I didn't think Donald Trump

00:01:59.119 --> 00:02:01.621
had the wit to conduct the coup.

00:02:01.955 --> 00:02:03.923
But now, having seen the history,

00:02:03.923 --> 00:02:05.959
if he's calling people into the streets

00:02:06.226 --> 00:02:06.993
this time, he's

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:09.262
seen the experience of January the sixth.

00:02:09.429 --> 00:02:10.930
And I think this is potentially

00:02:10.930 --> 00:02:11.798
very dangerous.

00:02:11.798 --> 00:02:12.765
So, again,

00:02:12.765 --> 00:02:14.701
people law enforcement in New York

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:16.236
obviously has to be concerned

00:02:16.236 --> 00:02:18.638
the safety of the citizens of New York.

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:20.940
But if something happens in this

00:02:21.274 --> 00:02:24.911
that allows Trump to make it into

00:02:24.911 --> 00:02:26.613
a campaign issue,

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.314
it's going to be very serious.

00:02:28.314 --> 00:02:28.681
I know,

00:02:28.681 --> 00:02:29.983
I know this must be

00:02:29.983 --> 00:02:31.784
galling to many people,

00:02:31.784 --> 00:02:32.785
but keep your eye on

00:02:32.785 --> 00:02:34.120
the ball, is what I'd say.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:35.922
If you don't want Donald Trump

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:36.689
to be elected

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:38.291
president again, for God

00:02:38.291 --> 00:02:40.059
sakes, be careful how you act.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:41.928
I get your point.

00:02:41.928 --> 00:02:42.462
I mean, I

00:02:42.462 --> 00:02:43.096
think I

00:02:43.096 --> 00:02:44.297
and I think he risks

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.832
surrendering the argument

00:02:45.832 --> 00:02:47.901
that this is a seven year old sex case

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.869
when if in fact,

00:02:49.869 --> 00:02:51.137
it should lead to protests.

00:02:51.137 --> 00:02:53.239
Hey, I like to respond to social media

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:54.107
in real time.

00:02:54.107 --> 00:02:54.474
Catherine,

00:02:54.474 --> 00:02:55.475
put something on the screen

00:02:55.475 --> 00:02:56.376
so that the ambassador

00:02:56.376 --> 00:02:58.444
and I can can answer it together.

00:02:58.912 --> 00:03:00.480
I'll read it aloud, Ambassador.

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:02.282
And he's calling for his minions

00:03:02.282 --> 00:03:04.184
to protest, says Gina.

00:03:04.184 --> 00:03:05.852
He was careful with his wording

00:03:05.852 --> 00:03:06.786
this time.

00:03:06.786 --> 00:03:09.556
He'll be out before his fingerprint ink

00:03:09.822 --> 00:03:13.293
can dry your thought

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.328
Well, he'll be out of the surrender

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:17.463
exercise on Tuesday, almost certainly.

00:03:17.463 --> 00:03:18.298
I mean, you go in,

00:03:18.298 --> 00:03:20.133
he's going to get his mug shot taken.

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:22.202
That that'll be interesting.

00:03:22.202 --> 00:03:24.737
And he'll be back in some safe location.

00:03:24.771 --> 00:03:26.339
We'll see what happens here.

00:03:26.339 --> 00:03:27.407
We'll see how many people

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:28.775
are willing to turn out for him.

00:03:28.775 --> 00:03:30.743
It may turn out to be a bust,

00:03:30.743 --> 00:03:32.845
but but I don't think law enforcement

00:03:32.845 --> 00:03:33.780
ought to do anything

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:35.648
that gives him an excuse to say

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:36.916
he's the most persecuted

00:03:36.916 --> 00:03:37.750
man in the world.

